::  GENERATED by tools/gen-perf-tests.py -- do not edit.
::
::  The tier-3 WORKLOAD SET (R2.8.1b). One workload per hot path, each
::  asserting the DETERMINISTIC WORK it does; the timing is read off the
::  runner's own `took` line by tools/tier3-noise.py and is deliberately not
::  asserted here -- R2.8.1a measured 0.9%-15.6% run-to-run on unchanged
::  code, so a time is not a fact a test can hold. What IS byte-reproducible
::  is the work, and that is what this file reports.
::
::  NOT A GATE. R2.8.1a's measurement decided tier 3 ships REPORT-ONLY:
::  `release-gate.sh` gets no clause from it. These arms fail only when the
::  port's own work profile CHANGES, which is a regression report, not a
::  threshold.
::
::  Budgets below are measured medians on vere 4.6, --loom 32, carried so a later
::  reader can tell a workload that got slower from one that was always slow.
/+  *test
/=  check  /lib/check
|%
++  prof
  ::  the full statistics of a SAFETY search: generated / distinct / queued /
  ::  depth, and the out-degree distribution the wire run-stats does not carry
  |=  [s=@t c=@t]
  ^-  [@ud @ud @ud @ud [@ud @ud @ud @ud]]
  (run-stats-full:check s c 0 1.000)
::
++  lprof
  ::  the LIVENESS workload's profile, and it is a different arm on purpose:
  ::  `+run-stats-full` builds `bfs-opts` with no liveness at all, so timing a
  ::  temporal spec through it measures the safety search and reports a fast,
  ::  meaningless number. Caught by this file's own capture -- the liveness
  ::  workload's profile came back as its 12-state safety graph. `+run-check`
  ::  is the entry point that actually reaches the 8.2-8.6 engine.
  ::  The leading digit is the verdict (1 = %ok), so a workload that starts
  ::  FAILING rather than merely getting slower shows up in the profile
  |=  [s=@t c=@t]
  ^-  [@ud @ud @ud @ud @ud]
  =/  r  (run-check:check s c 0)
  :-  ?:(?=(%ok -.-.r) 1 0)
  [generated.+.r distinct.+.r queued.+.r depth.+.r]
::
++  test-perf-enum
  ::  hot path: enumeration  (safety engine)
  ::  measured median: 1909 ms median of 15 runs (R2.8.1a: 5 warm + 5 fresh-boot + 5 post-rebuild)
  %+  expect-eq
    !>  [13 13 0 13 [0 1 1 1]]
  !>  (prof '---- MODULE A ----\0a\\* Hot path: ENUMERATION. SUBSET and \\X over small bases, forced inside a\0a\\* quantifier at every state -- the cursor / +force path, not the queue.\0aEXTENDS Integers\0aVARIABLE x\0aInit == x = 0\0aNext == x < 12 /\\ x\' = x + 1\0aInv  == /\\ \\A s \\in SUBSET (1..6) : Card1(s) >= 0\0a        /\\ \\A p \\in (1..8) \\X (1..8) : p[1] >= 1\0aCard1(s) == IF s = {} THEN 0 ELSE 1\0a====\0a' 'INIT Init\0aNEXT Next\0aINVARIANT Inv\0aCHECK_DEADLOCK FALSE\0a')
::
++  test-perf-eval
  ::  hot path: evaluator  (safety engine)
  ::  measured median: 1876 ms median of 15 runs (R2.8.1a: 5 warm + 5 fresh-boot + 5 post-rebuild)
  %+  expect-eq
    !>  [41 41 0 41 [0 1 1 1]]
  !>  (prof '---- MODULE A ----\0a\\* Hot path: the EVALUATOR. The state graph is a line, so almost all the time\0a\\* is +eval over a nested arithmetic/boolean invariant re-solved per state.\0aEXTENDS Integers\0aVARIABLE x\0aInit == x = 0\0aNext == x < 40 /\\ x\' = x + 1\0aHeavy(n) == ((n * n) + (n * 3) - 1) % 7\0aInv == /\\ Heavy(x) >= 0\0a       /\\ Heavy(x + 1) >= 0\0a       /\\ Heavy(x + 2) >= 0\0a       /\\ \\A i \\in 1..12 : Heavy(x + i) >= 0\0a====\0a' 'INIT Init\0aNEXT Next\0aINVARIANT Inv\0aCHECK_DEADLOCK FALSE\0a')
::
++  test-perf-fp
  ::  hot path: fingerprinting  (safety engine)
  ::  measured median: 2677 ms median of 15 runs (R2.8.1a: 5 warm + 5 fresh-boot + 5 post-rebuild)
  %+  expect-eq
    !>  [61 61 0 61 [0 1 1 1]]
  !>  (prof '---- MODULE A ----\0a\\* Hot path: FINGERPRINTING. Every state carries a record and a sequence, so\0a\\* each dedup pays a full structural +fp-enc rather than an integer one.\0aEXTENDS Integers, Sequences\0aVARIABLE r\0aInit == r = [a |-> 0, b |-> <<0, 0, 0>>, c |-> "z"]\0aNext == /\\ r.a < 60\0a        /\\ r\' = [a |-> r.a + 1,\0a                 b |-> <<r.a, r.a + 1, r.a + 2>>,\0a                 c |-> r.c]\0aInv  == r.a >= 0\0a====\0a' 'INIT Init\0aNEXT Next\0aINVARIANT Inv\0aCHECK_DEADLOCK FALSE\0a')
::
++  test-perf-live
  ::  hot path: liveness  (liveness engine)
  ::  measured median: 1106 ms median of 15 runs (R2.8.1a: 5 warm + 5 fresh-boot + 5 post-rebuild)
  %+  expect-eq
    !>  [1 13 12 0 12]
  !>  (lprof '---- MODULE A ----\0a\\* Hot path: LIVENESS. The 8.2-8.6 tableau build and lasso search, a\0a\\* different cost curve from the safety search.\0aEXTENDS Integers\0aVARIABLE x\0aInit == x = 0\0aNext == x\' = (x + 1) % 12\0aSpec == Init /\\ [][Next]_x /\\ WF_x(Next)\0aLive == <>(x = 11)\0a====\0a' 'SPECIFICATION Spec\0aPROPERTY Live\0a')
::
++  test-perf-queue
  ::  hot path: queue  (safety engine)
  ::  measured median: 2136 ms median of 15 runs (R2.8.1a: 5 warm + 5 fresh-boot + 5 post-rebuild)
  %+  expect-eq
    !>  [1.153 576 0 47 [0 1 1 2]]
  !>  (prof '---- MODULE A ----\0a\\* Hot path: the BFS QUEUE. A 24x24 grid walked one axis at a time -- many\0a\\* states carrying trivial values, so the cost is enqueue / dedup /\0a\\* fingerprint-set membership rather than evaluation.\0aEXTENDS Integers\0aVARIABLES x, y\0aInit == x = 0 /\\ y = 0\0aNext == \\/ /\\ x\' = (x + 1) % 24\0a           /\\ y\' = y\0a        \\/ /\\ y\' = (y + 1) % 24\0a           /\\ x\' = x\0aInv  == x < 24 /\\ y < 24\0a====\0a' 'INIT Init\0aNEXT Next\0aINVARIANT Inv\0a')
::
